{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1459158-question-can-garou-use-gifts-during-frenzy","id":1459158,"title":"Question: Can Garou use Gifts during Frenzy?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-09-07T11:25:43-07:00","id":1459158,"title":"Question: Can Garou use Gifts during Frenzy?","content":"Pretty much the title, can a frenzying Garou be able to use Gifts?<br /> If yes, what sort? I cant remember the source but I read Rage related Gifts can be used as Rage can be used normally during frenzy. If not, please let me know. <br /> thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12544-diplo","name":"diplo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12544_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-07T12:05:49-07:00","id":1459166,"title":"","content":"The rules are on page 261 of the W20 rulebook.<br /> <br /> A werewolf in frenzy can bite, claw, or run. He can spend Rage but only for extra actions. He can't split dice pools, use Gifts, or step sideways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-07T14:39:43-07:00","id":1459193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1459158-question-can-garou-use-gifts-during-frenzy?p=1459166#post1459166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rules are on page 261 of the W20 rulebook.<br /> <br /> A werewolf in frenzy can bite, claw, or run. He can spend Rage but only for extra actions. He can't split dice pools, use Gifts, or step sideways.</div> </div> </div> </div>Edit: NVM I found it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12376-mowtekpvp","user":"MowtekPvP","date":". 09-07-2021, 05:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12376-mowtekpvp","name":"MowtekPvP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-07T14:46:54-07:00","id":1459196,"title":"","content":"Black Fox stated a line from the cited page nearly verbatim. It's from the first paragraph after the Fox Frenzy passage.<br /> <br /> I would argue that &quot;use&quot; in this case likely means &quot;activate.&quot; I don't see why Frenzy would cause Spirit of the Fray to stop working, or already active Luna's Armor to turn off; the Garou doesn't need to consciously maintain Gift effects. But the rules are pretty clear cut that Frenzy precludes Garou doing anything that requires meaningful thought other than bite, claw, and run.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-08T01:29:09-07:00","id":1459263,"title":"","content":"I agree with Heavy Arms. Especially Gifts that are permanently in effect should stay in effect. Also Gifts that are activated before the Frenzy should stay in effect, for the most part.<br /> <br /> I think that frenzy usually bypasses wound penalties, but does not prohibit the rule about stunning when damage exceeds Stamina (which is unlikely due to the bonus to stamina in Crinos/Hispo, the only valid forms in frenzy). Still, imo a garou should in frenzy also be allowed to spend rage to ignore stun...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-08T02:52:33-07:00","id":1459265,"title":"","content":"Huh, I don't think I'd ever considered that issue... but by Stamina 3 most Garou in Frenzy can't be stunned without taking so much damage they'd be incapacitated anyway, I'm not sure how often it's ever had the chance to come up in play for me (and I've played a lot of WtA).<br /> <br /> That said, for Stamina 1-2 PCs, or Stamina 3 + Huge Size (or some other source of bonus health boxes), I'd allow that as well. I might even house rule that Frenzy flat out makes you immune to stun rather than worrying about Rage drain on the edge cases.<br /> <br /> It does seem important that one of the slight differences between Black Fox's statement and the book, is that the book says, &quot;He can spend Rage for extra actions, but can\u2019t split dice pools, use Gifts, or step sideways.&quot; The lack of &quot;only&quot; is generally superfluous, because resisting stun is pretty much the only thing to spend Rage on that isn't addressed. I'd be easily swayed that the more technically correct reading is that resisting stun isn't valid, but as I tend to side, I'll take what feels like the interpretation with the more satisfactory outcome over technical parsing if there's some leeway there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-08T03:27:30-07:00","id":1459270,"title":"","content":"Actually, come to think of it, I remember that the rules state a frenzy has to happen in Crinos or Hispo. So, I the garou in frenzy has his eyes on a target, and the target flees through an small opening, would the garou be able to spend Rage to instantly shift from Crinos to Hispo the pursue or would he start to break open the passage to fit through in Crinos.... given a scenario where there aren't other targets in sight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-08T03:54:04-07:00","id":1459272,"title":"","content":"The rules are that for a Berserk Frenzy you instantly shift to Crinos or Hispo (player choice), and for Fox Frenzy you shift to Lupus. Nothing suggests you can leave the starting form of the Frenzy until its over.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure how relevant being able to shift would be. If there's nothing to attack while berserking, that would generally be a trigger for the frenzy to start to subside rather than worrying about shifting from Hispo to Crinos to better deal with a door, or Crinos to Hispo to be faster and go running around for more targets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-09T08:21:14-07:00","id":1459436,"title":"","content":"I don't think a frenzied Garou would change forms further. That would be a lot of thinking, and the fact isn't that a frenzied Garou is stuck thinking like an animal, it is stuck at less than that. With everything else not an option, deciding to change forms for a more effective way of doing something is too much problem-solving.<br /> <br /> So I go with Heavy Arms, at this point it is a very good moment for the frenzy to start to subside. Or else &quot;door&quot; is a valid target at that point. Otherwise the Frenzy would just be excessively powerful even for this game and start to be a huge problem instead of a price to pay for sacred Rage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-09T11:16:29-07:00","id":1459452,"title":"","content":"Well, I would think not necessarily categorize a garou in frenzy as less than an animal. Controlled by rage and with the primary focus to destroy what ever triggered the frenzy the actions a garou can take are limited - no gifts and such, but the character still has perception and wits and should not be easily fooled by people pretending to be dead or hiding behind a bush. It is a slippery slope, but since it is up to the STs discretion what the Garou is allowed to do and what not, the ST is in control of how dangerous the frenzy really is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-09T14:04:45-07:00","id":1459468,"title":"","content":"No need to golden rule the argument, that goes without saying.<br /> <br /> But being unable to take actions similar to what is detailed in the rules is pretty much less than an animal can normally do. Few animals have reactions similar to the degree of thoughtless fury of a frenzy, and wolves aren't among them. I'm not saying that the character would be fooled by people feigning death, but not finding targets in the vicinity isn't the same.<br /> <br /> Do your senses tell you the corpse is actually feigning or that someone is hiding nearby? Great, target. But finding no one nearby and deciding to take out a door to go search, and not only that but figuring out the best form to do the job? If you find this congruent with uncontrollable rage, fine, but I don't. And I don't think this frenzy will be coherent with the level of danger alluded in the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-09T14:47:18-07:00","id":1459473,"title":"","content":"And, importantly, the rules to start rolling to end the Frenzy start when the instigating cause of the Frenzy is no longer present. A berserking Garou doesn't have to kill every valid target for some set period of time, once the target of their anger is either dead or beyond reach, the rolls start. Fox frenzy doesn't mean they just keep running and running until they pass out; just until they get away from whatever set them off.<br /> <br /> It's not even about &quot;fooling&quot; senses or something like that. If a Garou goes berserk over someone publicly humiliating them, and mauls the offender badly enough to cause them to run away or play dead, it's valid to say that the Garou's anger is sated by putting the insulting person in their place, and you can start rolling to get out of the Frenzy that soon (though until you succeed the violence isn't going to end).<br /> <br /> The ST's ruling on when the triggering stimulus is resolved is really the biggest factor on how dangerous the Frenzy is going to be. It could be a swift burst that only lasts a few seconds, or a rampage that takes half an hour to finally subside.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-09T19:51:50-07:00","id":1459489,"title":"","content":"If you want to be NICE Let people activate mercy In a frenzy to avoid killing people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-09T20:52:54-07:00","id":1459492,"title":"","content":"One of the explicit things CoGs use Mercy for is to activate it before they think they might be in a frenzy situation and don't want to murder people because they need to activate it before the frenzy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-09T22:22:39-07:00","id":1459497,"title":"","content":"oh when you spend WP to prevent a frenzy will someone see a glint in your eyes or something to give it away?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-09T22:39:18-07:00","id":1459499,"title":"","content":"Considering that it involves taking a full turn of centering and calming yourself, it's pretty hard to visualize it without having some sort of external signs.<br /> <br /> That said, nothing ever indicates you'd be able to tell the difference between a Garou just taking a moment to recenter because they're getting frustrated and don't want to Rage out, or one that's actively fighting off an imminent Frenzy.<br /> <br /> Safe bet would be, for characters that even know about Frenzies, an Empathy check should be able to spot things, but there's no specific tell that would automatically give it away. Of course, some Garou aren't necessarily going to bother hiding it if they lash out at something like punching a wall or slamming a door to shake off some of their growing anger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-09T23:20:09-07:00","id":1459505,"title":"","content":"To be fair, even someone who know nothing about frenzies would have a good chance at noticing that &quot;this dude is really upset&quot;. Any emotion strong enough to make you stop a full turn just to center yourself shouldn't be particularly hard to notice. I dare to say that any roll you call for hiding your emotions/reading emotions normally would have at least a +2/-2 in difficulty for this level of anger, or be automatically obvious to any one paying enough attention.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-10T01:31:27-07:00","id":1459523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1459158-question-can-garou-use-gifts-during-frenzy?p=1459468#post1459468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No need to golden rule the argument, that goes without saying.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't mean to invoke the Golden Rule. I misremembered (or remembered another edition) that the ST specifically has control over the character in a frenzy. And that is somewhat still in W20, although not as I recalled it. If the permanent Rage is exceeding the permanent Gnosis there is a need to spend Willpower to specifically choose who to rip apart. I quote:<br /> &quot;If he doesn\u2019t have the Willpower to spare, the Storyteller chooses who he attacks.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1459158-question-can-garou-use-gifts-during-frenzy?p=1459468#post1459468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... but not finding targets in the vicinity isn't the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. But my example/question above was about having found a target but being unable to reach it in Crinos, but being able to reach it in Hispo, which would both be acceptable forms for a berserk frenzy.<br /> Something like this:<br /> Step 1: Character falls into frenzy. Shifts to Crinos. Moves to attack.<br /> Step 2: Target ducks away and moves through a opening in a concrete wall..<br /> Step 3: Character in frenzy still knows where the target is, but can't follow.<br /> If the opening was passable in Hispo, the rules still wouldn't allow the garou to reach his target, because he was unable to shift. Had the player or ST shifted into Hispo in the first place, the outcome of the frenzy might be totally different. So an out-of-the-character decision made a huge in-game-impact (especially for the target, who might otherwise be dead).<br /> That is not to my liking, therefore I would advocate that a garou in frenzy should be able to spend Rage to shift forms if that would maximize his ability to inflict harm to a target creature.<br /> <br /> I hope this explains what I mean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-10T01:33:51-07:00","id":1459524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1459158-question-can-garou-use-gifts-during-frenzy?p=1459473#post1459473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And, importantly, the rules to start rolling to end the Frenzy start when the instigating cause of the Frenzy is no longer present. A berserking Garou doesn't have to kill every valid target for some set period of time, once the target of their anger is either dead or beyond reach, the rolls start.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but how would you handle it, if &quot;beyond reach&quot; means flying overhead, being on a monitor, being behind steel bars or some similar hindrance, but still taunting you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-10T01:36:44-07:00","id":1459525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1459158-question-can-garou-use-gifts-during-frenzy?p=1459497#post1459497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">oh when you spend WP to prevent a frenzy will someone see a glint in your eyes or something to give it away?</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with the posts above. I would allow rolls to hide the emotion tells as well as perception + empathy to notice them anyway. In most circumstances, it would be noticeable right away, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-10T03:02:51-07:00","id":1459528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1459158-question-can-garou-use-gifts-during-frenzy?p=1459523#post1459523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope this explains what I mean.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that made things clearer.<br /> <br /> Personally, though, my interpretation of the Frenzy would still be the same. As a raging beast I picture the Garou simply trying to overpower its way to the target in &quot;a straight line&quot;. Like rending concrete and stone, jumping and climbing. Again, I interpret evaluating the situation and Changing to accommodate as beyond the capacity of a frenzied Garou for focus. Hence why I have no qualms with the limitation on using Rage to Change.<br /> <br /> But in such scenarios I wouldn't have a big problem with your interpretation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-10T03:55:09-07:00","id":1459536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1459158-question-can-garou-use-gifts-during-frenzy?p=1459524#post1459524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True, but how would you handle it, if &quot;beyond reach&quot; means flying overhead, being on a monitor, being behind steel bars or some similar hindrance, but still taunting you.</div> </div> </div> </div>In a way that my players don't feel like I'm being an ass.<br /> <br /> Theorizing is fun and all, but I think we can agree there's a point where the rules are never perfect, and whatever we come up with for the thread on what might be the most accurate interpretation of the text doesn't really matter because actually doing it in play to your players would be cruel, or if your players are doing this sort of thing on purpose they probably have other things to worry about... like all the punishment rites that they're going to get smacked with. If the players are in a situation that only exists to provoke a Frenzy and not let them at least rip up the jerk tormenting them.... what's the point of that when playing the game?<br /> <br /> If for some reason I was really pressed to give an answer? I wouldn't even call for a roll. Frenzy is a magically exaggerated flight or fight response. A threat that's too separated from you to be in danger of you when you Frenzy is too separated to rile up Rage enough to make you roll for Frenzy. Lions on TV are scary, but they don't activate my adrenal responses because they're just on TV. Even my deep primordial lizard brain knows there's no threat and doesn't kick survival mode on.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-10T06:16:27-07:00","id":1459547,"title":"","content":"Hm... problem is, that Rage roll triggers are any emotions really, not just threats, and humiliation is a named trigger. If that changes once you entered the frenzy, well, I don't think so.<br /> <br /> Also, it's not something I'd do to a player - although it isn't just a thought experiment either.<br /> <br /> A Ragabash once used the Uktena &quot;air walk&quot;-like Gift to be out of reach and taunt another players character. It was to make a point of him being easy to frenzy and therefore being a liability. The frenzied garou randomly picked up sticks and stones to throw at the Ragabash, for I ruled, even in a frenzy this should be a more appropriate reaction than tearing apart a random plant - because no other suitable targets were around - spirit witnesses on the other side of the Gauntlet were obviously out of reach. Also, packmates weren't an option, for permanent Gnosis exceeded permanent Rage and not the other way round.<br /> <br /> Would you slap the Ragabash with a punishment rite in such a situation, or award renown for pointing out another garou's weakness in a way that didn't leave anyone hurt?<br /> <br /> The whole situation was of course even more of an discussion, because the Ragabash in LARP wasn't really flying, and no foam stone equivalents were available. Even if there were some, they would have to be soaked in water to be able to be thrown properly and it was freezing outside... But that's only a side note.<br /> <br /> In fact, our LARP distinguishes between a targeted berserker frenzy and an unfocused berserker frenzy. The targeted berserker frenzy happens, if you have a direct reason to frenzy, and in that case you have a primary target. Also that target isn't allowed to use mind-control or emotion-control powers on the frenzied garou - except these explicitly state they work on targets in frenzy. Once the target is destroyed or if the frenzy emerged from a situation without an clear source of the frenzy, then the garou attacks the next suitable target. This unfocused frenzy ends after a predetermined per-character individual while - simulation how a character would roll willpower until the successes to end the frenzy are achieved. The targeted berserker frenzy however doesn't end unless the player is to exhausted to continue, for it assumes the reason for the frenzy is still there and as per the tabletop rules Willpower rolls to end the frenzy aren't allowed yet.<br /> <br /> We also allow that targeted frenzy is allowed against significant objects, is on the scene, although they wouldn't last long. But, if you are on a zoom call and get the news that your kinfolk family was murdered, the laptop gets the first attack before any other target. Some would go for some cursed fetish that caused something that triggers the frenzy. It felt that such an option would make sense in the overall drama - and since the objects are gone basically immediately the frenzy doesn't lose its danger to the other characters around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-10T12:09:56-07:00","id":1459573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1459158-question-can-garou-use-gifts-during-frenzy?p=1459547#post1459547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm... problem is, that Rage roll triggers are any emotions really, not just threats, and humiliation is a named trigger.</div> </div> </div> </div>And all Rage rolls that exist just to check for Frenzy are at the ST's discretion. It's the ST's call if something is humiliating enough, a strong enough emotion, and taunt that gets under the skin enough, to even justify rolling in the first place. The slightest twinge of emotions aren't automatic triggers for Frenzy rolls.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Would you slap the Ragabash with a punishment rite in such a situation, or award renown for pointing out another garou's weakness in a way that didn't leave anyone hurt? </div> </div> </div>Both. Because the Ragabash got lucky. There's no way for the characters to know what another character's mechanical ratings in Rage and Gnosis are. What if the Ragabash had driven their target into Thrall instead of just a normal berserk, leading to a packmate's death? What if some uninvolved NPC stumbled across things and was suddenly the only valid target? What about the risks of leaving a warrior of Gaia drained of their will in a fashion that could take days to recover, and thus denying the Sept/etc. a fighter that might be needed at any minute? Whatever value there is in taking a Garou that's not honest about their ability to control their Rage down a peg has to be weighed against how dangerous it is to provoke a Frenzy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In fact, our LARP distinguishes between a targeted berserker frenzy and an unfocused berserker frenzy.... </div> </div> </div>House rules are cool, but that means we're beyond thought experiments about what's in the books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-10T16:56:42-07:00","id":1459599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1459158-question-can-garou-use-gifts-during-frenzy?p=1459573#post1459573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And all Rage rolls that exist just to check for Frenzy are at the ST's discretion. It's the ST's call if something is humiliating enough, a strong enough emotion, and taunt that gets under the skin enough, to even justify rolling in the first place. The slightest twinge of emotions aren't automatic triggers for Frenzy rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>In theory.<br /> But what do you do, if players want to roll their rage, because they find something another PC said 'enraging'? And of cause they are curious if they will enter frenzy and how that might turn the story. Especially if the troupe is rather new and hasn't played that long together.<br /> Do you forbid it? Do you ignore it if they already picked up their dices and rolled them?<br /> <br /> The difficulties for Rage rolls are one big problem in WtA in my opinion, for they vary to much. IMO Full Moon should be diff 5, new moon diff 7 and all other phases 6. But that is a side note...<br /> <br /> And if the PC is taunting. What if the character with <i>Persuasion</i> and 5 successes on a Manipulation + Expression roll is taunting. Shouldn't that have an effect, even on another PC? Isn't there a need to fullfil the players expectations....<br /> <br /> In our LARP game, we have for most social interactions a &quot;victim rule&quot;, meaning that the person who is affected by a social action (or supernatural effect) has a lot of leeway on depicting if and how strong the effect is on the character. In a tabletop game, the interpretation of a roll might fall to the ST, however...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1459158-question-can-garou-use-gifts-during-frenzy?p=1459573#post1459573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Both. Because the Ragabash got lucky.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then another Ragabash might play a trick on him to proof he was reckless.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1459158-question-can-garou-use-gifts-during-frenzy?p=1459573#post1459573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> There's no way for the characters to know what another character's mechanical ratings in Rage and Gnosis are</div> </div> </div> </div>True. But that the garou in question didn't attack his packmates in previous frenzies as well as being able to recall what happened during the frenzy was well documented.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1459158-question-can-garou-use-gifts-during-frenzy?p=1459573#post1459573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if the Ragabash had driven their target into Thrall instead of just a normal berserk, leading to a packmate's death?</div> </div> </div> </div>That would still prove the Ragabash's point, however unfortunate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1459158-question-can-garou-use-gifts-during-frenzy?p=1459573#post1459573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if some uninvolved NPC stumbled across things and was suddenly the only valid target? What about the risks of leaving a warrior of Gaia drained of their will in a fashion that could take days to recover, and thus denying the Sept/etc. a fighter that might be needed at any minute?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that were circumstances that were reasonably not likely to occur.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1459158-question-can-garou-use-gifts-during-frenzy?p=1459573#post1459573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whatever value there is in taking a Garou that's not honest about their ability to control their Rage down a peg has to be weighed against how dangerous it is to provoke a Frenzy.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. In the given situation however (meaning I know the physical place, likely hood of anyone coming across the scene, etc.), I wouldn't rule the Ragabash as negligent in that regard.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1459158-question-can-garou-use-gifts-during-frenzy?p=1459573#post1459573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">House rules are cool, but that means we're beyond thought experiments about what's in the books.</div> </div> </div> </div>True.<br /> But, as our LARP rules were created, there was a deeply held believe from vampire LARP converts, that a supernatural being in was immune to mind- or emotion-affecting powers while in frenzy. This wasn't true for vamprie revised (where there is a +2 difficulty, iirc) and not even heard of in WtA.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-10T19:45:33-07:00","id":1459612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1459158-question-can-garou-use-gifts-during-frenzy?p=1459599#post1459599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In theory.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, in the rules. It's not in theory, it's how the game is meant to be played: The ST decides if the situation calls for a roll or not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But what do you do, if players want to roll their rage, because they find something another PC said 'enraging'? And of cause they are curious if they will enter frenzy and how that might turn the story. Especially if the troupe is rather new and hasn't played that long together.<br /> Do you forbid it? Do you ignore it if they already picked up their dices and rolled them? </div> </div> </div>Especially for a newer troupe I'd rule against it. Frenzies happen easily enough in the system, you don't need to &quot;try it out.&quot; If they don't know the system well, they're unlikely to be considering things like &quot;you lose Renown now&quot; as Frenzies are a Renown hit, or no the odds of a Frenzy or Thrall are.<br /> <br /> And all of my players know I don't care if they rolled dice already. I make it clear in session zero for any new player that rolls I didn't either call for or assent to don't count. Since factors players might not be aware of can change dice-pools, I want to make sure players don't have to reroll because I was going to toss a dice-pool modifier at something; such as saying that the character got hit with addition Temp. Rage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Isn't there a need to fullfil the players expectations.... </div> </div> </div>There's a need to acknowledge player expectations... fulfilling them is less clear cut.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Then another Ragabash might play a trick on him to proof he was reckless. </div> </div> </div>That too. But the Philodox have the duty to enforce the rules and peace of Garou gatherings. Smacking down a Garou that's provoking Frenzies is something most Philodox aren't going to struggle with deciding is necessary.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That would still prove the Ragabash's point, however unfortunate. </div> </div> </div>Not really. Any Garou can be driven to have enough Temp. Rage to Frenzy, or even Thrall, assuming they don't have the Perm. Rage to do that already. Unless the target has a Flaw or something that reduces the difficulty to Frenzy, what was really proven? Esp. the more Gifts being used to pull it off.<br /> <br /> Why not provoke a Fox Frenzy which is far less dangerous?<br /> <br /> Basically, I'm not convinced to worry about this sort of situation, even if it happened in one of your games, because I'm not seeing it as something that is compelling to allow or encourage as something to expect in play.<br /> <br /> &quot;Don't be a dick, even if your character is one.&quot; is a basic rule for my games.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-11T00:02:59-07:00","id":1459630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1459158-question-can-garou-use-gifts-during-frenzy?p=1459612#post1459612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, in the rules. It's not in theory, it's how the game is meant to be played: The ST decides if the situation calls for a roll or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh... you are right. All Rage rolls are at the Storyteller's discretion. Except for those called for by a Gift activation and such.<br /> <br /> Possibly I have dealt with too many players who made and wanted to make that call for themselves...<br /> Also, I'm influenced a lot by LARP where the players have to make calls<br /> <br /> Thanks for pointing that out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1459158-question-can-garou-use-gifts-during-frenzy?p=1459612#post1459612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Especially for a newer troupe I'd rule against it. Frenzies happen easily enough in the system, you don't need to &quot;try it out.&quot; If they don't know the system well, they're unlikely to be considering things like &quot;you lose Renown now&quot; as Frenzies are a Renown hit, or no the odds of a Frenzy or Thrall are.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. Although in my mind I was talking about Players with experience in the game, but never before having played in that constellation and with those characters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1459158-question-can-garou-use-gifts-during-frenzy?p=1459612#post1459612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And all of my players know I don't care if they rolled dice already. I make it clear in session zero for any new player that rolls I didn't either call for or assent to don't count. Since factors players might not be aware of can change dice-pools, I want to make sure players don't have to reroll because I was going to toss a dice-pool modifier at something; such as saying that the character got hit with addition Temp. Rage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good Call,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1459158-question-can-garou-use-gifts-during-frenzy?p=1459612#post1459612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a need to acknowledge player expectations... fulfilling them is less clear cut.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also true.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1459158-question-can-garou-use-gifts-during-frenzy?p=1459612#post1459612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really. Any Garou can be driven to have enough Temp. Rage to Frenzy, or even Thrall, assuming they don't have the Perm. Rage to do that already. Unless the target has a Flaw or something that reduces the difficulty to Frenzy, what was really proven? Esp. the more Gifts being used to pull it off.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but the point was, that it was easy to do it, not that the Ragabash had to invest much time or effort.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}